      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقترض</span></b>  <i>He received what is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْض</span> [<i>a
loan,</i> or <i>the like</i>], (S, Msb, K,) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَلَفَ</span>; (A;)
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْهُ</span> <i>from him.</i> (S, A, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقترض عِرْضَهُ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>He
defamed him,</i> or <i>spoke evil of him, behind his
back</i> or <i>in his absence,</i> or <i>otherwise;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِغْتَابَهُ</span>:
(K:) as though he cut off [somewhat] from his
honour. (TA.)

